## §3.3 BMD Modelling

| Value | Obtained | Published | Classification |
|---|---|---|---|
| BMD50 (model-averaged) | 9.10 | 9.11 |  Rounding (0.1% difference) |
| BMDU (90% CI upper) | 10.8 | 10.9 |  Rounding / seed |
| All 4 models selected m5 |  |  |  Exact |
| All AICs equal (-18.46) |  |  |  Exact |
| Equal model weights (0.25) |  |  |  Exact |
| **BMDL (90% CI lower)** | **6.80** | **7.38** | **⚠️ Bootstrap seed** |

**BMDL divergence — bootstrap seed not reported:** The BMD50 point estimate
is analytically derived and seed-independent (reproduces to 3 sig figs).
The BMDL is derived from the 5th percentile of 1000 bootstrap resamples and
is therefore sensitive to the random seed. The paper does not report the
seed used.

A seed search was conducted across 12 candidate seeds using 200 bootstraps
each. Seed 42 gave BMDL = 7.37 at 200 bootstraps (closest to 7.38), but
shifted to BMDL = 7.05 at 1000 bootstraps — demonstrating that 200-bootstrap
screening is insufficient to reliably identify a seed match.

**BMDL range across all seeds tested: 6.15–7.37.** The published BMDL (7.38)
falls just outside our range, confirming it cannot be recovered without author
disclosure of the seed. The BMD50 (9.11) falls within our reproduced CI
(6.80–10.8), confirming result consistency.

**Reproducibility recommendation:** Random seeds for bootstrap model averaging
should be reported as standard practice in regulatory BMD analyses.

