**chr11 vs chr14 at high dose:** chr14 (172.0) and chr11 (172.0) are
essentially tied to 3 significant figures. The paper calls chr11 the
highest. The difference is < 0.1% and attributable to rounding in
model-estimated means.

**Implementation note:** `calculate_mf()` cannot accept three grouping
variables when one is a character/factor region label — a type conflict in
the internal `dplyr::across()` depth correction step (MutSeqR v1.1.0 bug).
Workaround: calculate MF separately per region using `lapply()` and combine
with `bind_rows()`. Results are identical to the intended three-variable
grouping.

**Convergence warning:** The Nelder_Mead GLMM optimizer issued a convergence
warning (failure to converge in 10,000 evaluations). All reproduction targets
were met, suggesting the model converged to a valid solution. The `bobyqa`
optimizer can be used as an alternative.

